    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **286 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented a daily owner-registration cap that rejects creating an owner once 20 owners already carry today's registration date, returning HTTP 400.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`DailyOwnerRegistrationLimitException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` marking that the daily limit was hit, in the `rest.advice` package alongside the existing `DuplicateOwnerException`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 20` constant and an `isDailyRegistrationLimitReached()` helper that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()`. In `addOwner`, after defaulting the registration date, it throws the new exception when the count is \u2265 20. The check runs before the duplicate checks so the limit is enforced regardless of the candidate's other fields.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DailyOwnerRegistrationLimitException` that returns a `400 Bad Request` `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the style of the existing handlers.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`** \u2014 added a `registerOwnersToday(count)` helper and two tests: one confirming the 21st creation is rejected with 400 when 20 owners are registered today, and a boundary test confirming creation still succeeds at 19.\n\nThe rule counts by registration date against the current day, so it naturally resets at midnight, and seed owners (which have null registration dates) don't count toward today's tally.",
